From 14c8542159db80ca7f48163351450fc5c83d3dd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron N <aaronna@valvesoftware.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:22:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: apply STA bandwidth limit before channel
 setup

Restrict chanreq->oper to conn->bw_limit in ieee80211_determine_chan_mode() so
the initial chanctx and the stored TPE use the station width.

Without this a STA limited to 160 MHz sets up the AP's 320 MHz
channel and TPE, then downgrades after the association response
with that stale 16 level TPE still in place. In the top 320 MHz block
this caused ath12k to walk past the last 6 GHz channel and oops on a NULL
channel lookup.
---
 net/mac80211/mlme.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/mac80211/mlme.c b/net/mac80211/mlme.c
index fa773f3b0541..f6179420bc8e 100644
--- a/net/mac80211/mlme.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/mlme.c
@@ -1333,6 +1333,11 @@ again:
 
 	ieee80211_set_chanreq_ap(sdata, chanreq, conn, ap_chandef);
 
+	/* apply the station's limit before channel setup and TPE rearrangement */
+	while (conn->bw_limit <
+	       ieee80211_min_bw_limit_from_chandef(&chanreq->oper))
+		ieee80211_chandef_downgrade(&chanreq->oper, NULL);
+
 	while (!ieee80211_chandef_usable(sdata, &chanreq->oper,
 					 IEEE80211_CHAN_DISABLED)) {
 		if (chanreq->oper.width == NL80211_CHAN_WIDTH_20_NOHT) {
-- 
